      "artist": "WishywizPH",
      "description": "This Photo was taken in Philippine national Museum\nContext: \n\"Church Architecture of Cebu\"\n\nChurch architecture was a necessity for the evangelization of the Filipino people during Spanish colonial rule. Churches also served political and practical purposes that furthered the development of communities. Before the arrival of the Spaniards, Filipino natives used light construction materials; early churches were designed the same way until innovations led to the use of stone and masonry to create more long-lasting structures. Cebu's history can be traced to the founding of the Basilica Minore del Santo Niño de Cebu, which legend says was the site where an image of the Holy Child was discovered, and Miguel Lopez de Legazpi established the first Spanish settlement in the area of the discovery soon after.",
