      "artist": "WishywizPH",
      "description": "Planning any Spanish colonial-era settlement emphasized defense, particularly to scare off Moro raiders and other dangers. When stone constructions of churches became typical, it was then able to be used as defensible structures, with their prime location, large scale, and prominence The Church of Our Lady of Patrocinio in Boljoon, Cebu, is a fine example of a church used as a defensive structure. Constructed in 1599, the fortress church is on a hill overlookıng the sea, allowing it to give early warning against Moro raiders The church also features bell towers that were used as watchtowers and overall presents an austere, unadorned architectural volume and exterior constructed of locally quarried coral stone topped with a roof of terracotta tiles",
      "dateCreated": "2024-11-28 14:45:05",
